{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q849"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_758826587#9_1527255102","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q849","rank":3,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_758826587#9_1527255102\" , \"end_char\": 8086.000000 , \"headings\": \"Two Minutes Hate 1984 1984 Two Minutes Hate <cover>1984 Expert Answers Further Reading We’ll help your grades soar \" , \"segment\": \"The politicians will invent an enemy and then channel the public rage against that enemy. Approved by eNotes Editorial Team Isabell Schimmel Educator since 2012 35,398 answers | Certified Educator Page Citation Share Link The Two Minutes Hate is a daily ritual performed by the members of the party in the book's dystopian society. During the Two Minutes Hate, the party members watch films of people like Goldstein who are enemies of the Party. They scream in hatred </cover>at these people. The purpose of this is to help make the people lose their individuality. They are all supposed to show the same emotions about the same things at the same time. It makes them feel that they and everyone else all feel the same -- and that these feelings are what the Party tells them to have. Approved by eNotes Editorial Team We’","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_758826587#7_1527251764","rank":2,"relevance":3}]}}
