{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_758826587#9_1527255102","relevance":3,"reason":"The passage directly explains the Two Minutes Hate as a Party ritual in which members scream hatred at Goldstein and other enemies, with the purpose of erasing individuality and making everyone display and feel the same Party-directed emotions. This directly supports hatred as a tool for collective unity/conformity in 1984.","learned":"The Two Minutes Hate unites people by making them express identical hatred at the same time, reducing individuality and aligning emotions with Party commands."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q849","reason":"This result list is producing direct evidence about the Party channeling hatred and enforcing collective emotion; continue for more potentially grade-3 passages."}}
