{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"1984\" goldstein \"common enemy\" (+ citizens party people unite unity))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_873931060#13_1477672176","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q853","rank":1,"snippet":"char\": 8220.000000 , \"headings\": \"1984 Summary and Analysis of Part Two VIII-X 1984 by George Orwell<cover>1984 Summary and Analysis of Part Two VIII-X \" , \"segment\": \"Each country still builds and hoards atomic bombs, which were developed long before the superstates were established. Oceania is ruled under the ideology of Ingsoc, Eurasia under Neo-Bolshevism, and Eastasia under what can be translated as either \\\"Death-worship\\\" or \\\"Obliteration of the Self.\\\" All countries have an Inner Party, a Party, a prole structure, and worship absolute, semi-divine leaders. Goldstein states, \\\"when war becomes literally continuous, it also ceases to be dangerous...technical progress can cease and the most palpable facts can be denied or disregarded.\\\" The people have no way of knowing the true state of the world, and must rely entirely upon the Party. Rather than being a war between nations, the war is waged upon the people to maintain loyalty, unity against a common enemy, </cover>and Party domination. Thus, as war maintains order in each individual nation, the meaning of the Party slogan \"War is Peace\" becomes clear. Julia arrives, briefly acknowledges "}}
{"request":{"judgments":"21/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_873931060#13_1477672176","relevance":3,"reason":"The passage directly explains that in 1984 perpetual war is waged on the people to maintain loyalty, unity against a common enemy, and Party domination. This is strong direct evidence that hatred/opposition toward an enemy is used to unite people under the Party.","learned":"Goldstein's account of perpetual war shows that the Party maintains loyalty and unity by keeping citizens oriented against a common enemy."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q853","reason":"This common-enemy/Goldstein query produced direct grade-3 evidence about unity against a shared enemy; continue for additional relevant results from the same focused list."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q853"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_873931060#14_1477673807","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q853","rank":2,"snippet":"\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_873931060#14_1477673807\" , \"end_char\": 8965.000000 , \"headings\": \"1984 Summary and Analysis of Part Two VIII-X 1984 by George Orwell<cover>1984 Summary and Analysis of Part Two VIII-X \" , \"segment\": \"Rather than being a war between nations, the war is waged upon the people to maintain loyalty, unity against a common enemy, and Party domination. Thus, as war maintains order in each individual nation, the meaning of the Party slogan \\\"War is Peace\\\" becomes clear. Julia arrives, briefly acknowledges the book, and busies herself making coffee. Half an hour later, while lying in bed, Winston tells Julia she must also read the book, and she asks him to read it aloud so that they can both take it in at the same time. He begins again at the first chapter. Goldstein </cover>discusses the pyramidal shape of society, which consists of the High, who wish to remain high, Middle, who wish to change places with the high, and Low, who wish to develop a society based on equality among all men. When the Middle "}}
